{"content":[{"c":["AMMIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Gemalli’s son, one of 12 men sent by Moses to spy out the land of Canaan. Ammiel represented Dan’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.12","r":"Num.13.12","rawR":"Num.13.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.12","value":"Num.13.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 13:12"},") and later died because of a plague (",{"href":"?bref=Num.14.37","r":"Num.14.37","rawR":"Num.14.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.14.37","value":"Num.14.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 14:37"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Father of Machir of Lo-debar. Mephibosheth, Jonathan’s son, was hidden from David in Machir’s house (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.9.4-5","r":"2Sam.9.4-5","rawR":"2Sam.9.4-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.9.4-5","value":"2Sam.9.4-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 9:4-5"},"). Machir later helped supply David in his war with Absalom (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.27-29","r":"2Sam.17.27-29","rawR":"2Sam.17.27-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.27-29","value":"2Sam.17.27-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 17:27-29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Father of David’s wife, Bath-shua (or Bathsheba, ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.5","r":"1Chr.3.5","rawR":"1Chr.3.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.5","value":"1Chr.3.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:5"},"). Ammiel is also called Eliam (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.11.3","r":"2Sam.11.3","rawR":"2Sam.11.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.11.3","value":"2Sam.11.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 11:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Sixth son of Obed-edom, who, along with his family, served as gatekeeper in the temple during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.5,15","r":"1Chr.26.5,15","rawR":"1Chr.26.5,15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.5,15","value":"1Chr.26.5,15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:5, 15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ammiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 13:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.12","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.12","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.12"},{"anchorText":"Nm 14:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.14.37","rawQueryValue":"Num.14.37","sourceRefExact":"Num.14.37"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 9:4-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.9.4-5","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.9.4-5","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.9.4-5"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 17:27-29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.27-29","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.17.27-29","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.17.27-29"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.5"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 11:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.11.3","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.11.3","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.11.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:5, 15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.5,15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.5,15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.5,15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"af95a1f4ca6ffefe6ff0a757778d63356645f4be90d90f18db5a70a93d63c5ae","sourceItemName":"Ammiel","sourceItemOrder":300,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ammiel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ammiel","title":"Ammiel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}